Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 00:45:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] TUI footer background tasks indicator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a "● N bg" indicator to the home footer reporting how many
background-mode Task children are currently running across all parents.
Sits between LiveSessions and HivemindStatus.

Mechanism mirrors the LiveSessions component (patch 0012):
  - onMount fetches Global.backgroundTasks() (added to the SDK by
    the matching dep_patch) for initial state.
  - api.event.on("session.background.changed", ...) drives reactive
    updates from the engine's bus event (patch 0017).
  - Only `running` entries count toward the indicator —
    completed-but-unconsumed results are the model's concern (it sees
    them as a <system-reminder> on its next turn) not the user's.
  - Bullet uses theme().success when count > 0, theme().textMuted when
    zero, matching the existing convention.

No polling. No new SSE channel — the existing /event stream already
carries bus events, this component just listens for one more variant.
